# DocMind Mobile — Flutter Conventions

## Architecture: Clean Architecture per Feature

Every feature lives in `lib/features/<feature>/` with three layers:

```
lib/features/<feature>/
├── data/
│   ├── datasources/     # remote API calls (Dio) and local storage
│   ├── dtos/            # JSON-serializable DTOs
│   └── repositories/    # concrete repository implementations
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/        # plain Dart classes, no framework deps
│   ├── repositories/    # abstract interfaces
│   ├── usecases/        # one class per use case
│   └── failures/        # domain failure types
└── presentation/
    ├── pages/           # full-screen widgets
    ├── widgets/         # feature-specific reusable widgets
    └── controllers/     # GetX controllers (state + business logic bridge)
```

**Dependency direction**: `presentation` → `domain` ← `data` (data depends on domain interfaces)

## State Management & DI — GetX

- Use `GetX` / `Obx` for reactive UI; bind controllers via `Get.put` or `Get.lazyPut`
- Controllers go in `presentation/controllers/`; they call use cases, not repositories directly
- Route to new pages with `Get.toNamed(AppRoutes.routeName)`; define all named routes in `lib/core/routes/app_routes.dart`

```dart
// ✅ GOOD — controller calls use case
class AuthController extends GetxController {
  final LoginUseCase _loginUseCase;
  AuthController(this._loginUseCase);

  Future<void> login(String email, String password) async {
    final result = await _loginUseCase(email, password);
    result.fold((failure) => ..., (user) => ...);
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — controller calls repository directly
class AuthController extends GetxController {
  final AuthRepository _repo; // skip use case layer
}
```

## HTTP — Dio Client

- All API calls go through `lib/core/network/dio_client.dart`
- Base URL and endpoint constants live in `lib/core/api_constants.dart` — never hardcode URLs elsewhere
- Handle errors in the data layer; return `Either<Failure, T>` from repositories (using `dartz` or similar)
- Attach auth token in the Dio interceptor; do not pass tokens manually per call

## Naming Conventions

| Layer | Suffix | Example |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Use cases | `_usecase.dart` | `login_usecase.dart` |
| DTOs | `_dto.dart` | `user_dto.dart` |
| Controllers | `_controller.dart` | `auth_controller.dart` |
| Repositories (abstract) | `_repository.dart` | `auth_repository.dart` |
| Implementations | `_repository_impl.dart` | `auth_repository_impl.dart` |
| Pages | `_page.dart` | `login_page.dart` |

- Dart files: `snake_case`; classes: `PascalCase`; variables/methods: `camelCase`

## Shared Core (`lib/core/`)

- `network/` — Dio client, interceptors
- `routes/` — `AppRoutes` named route constants
- `theme/` — colors, text styles, spacing tokens
- Do not put feature-specific code in `core/`; keep it truly shared

## Adding a New Feature

1. Create `lib/features/<name>/` with all three layer folders
2. Define domain entities and abstract repository in `domain/`
3. Write use cases (one per operation) in `domain/usecases/`
4. Implement repository + DTOs + datasource in `data/`
5. Wire GetX controller + pages in `presentation/`
6. Register routes in `app_routes.dart` and bind controller in the binding class
